horizon zero dawn guerrillas ambitious  open-world game is finally out in the  wild and it's pretty damn cool if you've  made it to the desert by now you've  probably gotten a taste of some of the  bigger deadlier machines the game has to  offer if you're getting your ass kicked  in the early game check out our  essential tips video and make sure to  subscribe for more on horizon  but if you're looking for an edge on  taking down some of the most dangerous  machines then look no further  before we get into the nitty-gritty  let's get some of the basics out of the  way first make sure your medicine pouch  is topped off even if you are over  leveled one well-placed hit can knock a  LOI on her ass make sure to have potions  ready and an ample supply of tare blast  and hardpoint arrows if you don't know  if those are then you might want to buy  a new bow by now you should have the  hunter reflex and concentration perks  but if you don't unlock them I'd also  recommend concentration plus and fast  reload and remember it's smart to  checkout the Machine catalog or scan it  with your focus before going toe to toe  with one of these behemoths now that  we're all stocked up on supplies let's  lay some machines Sarah Connor style  we're gonna kick this off with the rock  breaker one-on-one these guys aren't too  tough unfortunately apart from a side  quest I've yet to find one of these  things alone they usually come in pairs  and if you aren't constantly moving and  checking your surroundings you won't  last long when you engage a pair of rock  breakers keep your eyes on the ground  you should see dirt flying up in the air  as they burrow around the battlefield  keep rolling into one of these creatures  reveals itself once they're out in the  open you have a few options you can  shoot its arms disabling its ability to  dig you can destroy the fuel sack  disabling its ranged attacks or you can  shoot the exhaust vent I typically don't  go for the arms because you have to  destroy all four in order to stop the  rock breaker from digging however if the  opportunity to shoot the fuel sack  arises I'd recommend lodging a few  well-placed hardpoint or precision  arrows in its stomach because its range  attacks can be deadly and tough to avoid  this leaves the exhaust port I focused  most my fire here because it deals a  hefty bit of damage and it's a  relatively easy target to hit once  you've eliminated the first rock breaker  the second shouldn't be too tough  next let's take a look at the storm bird  these things are deadly somewhat common  and tough to hit if you've spent more  than a few hours in a desert there's a  good chance you've run into one if  you're still using a basic bow I'd avoid  this confrontation altogether however if  you're feeling brave there are some  techniques that can ground these birds  first you'll need to take out its  lightning gun with a tear arrow or two  these machines can carpet the  battlefield with electricity and fire  devastating balls of energy after that  stun wait until a bird lands when it  touches down pin it to the ground with  the rope castor and aim for its blaze  canisters with your fire arrows by now  you should know what happens when you  set one of these puppies ablaze in most  cases though that won't kill it from  here  I either aim for the freeze canisters  located on its shoulders or the engines  on its wings work it down a little more  and the storm bird should fall a quick  side note when you are fighting a storm  bird it's easy to focus on what's above  you rather than what's around you this  makes it easy for smaller machines to  get in your way so be careful  finally let's take a look at the Thunder  job  if you've been watching trailers and  demos of horizon you'll probably  recognize this bipedal machine it's  probably one of the toughest machines to  take down in the game it has a couple  weak points but getting to them can be  kind of tricky so make sure you have  tear blast arrows ready before you  engage once you find yourself staring  down one of these things I'd aim for all  of your little toys disable the disc  launcher knock off the radar and rip off  its cannons these machines have a wide  range of moves so blowing off its  weapons can eliminate a lot of its  strategies but that's never enough fire  a tear blast  arrow right in its noggin to reveal its  data Nexus this is a little square chip  that if hit directly deals a lot of  damage the catch is that it's on top of  its head so unless you have high ground  or the Beast is looking down it can be  difficult to hit if you're having  trouble hitting that you can aim for  either side of its neck with a tear  blast arrow to reveal its heart the  heart is a bit tougher to get to but  it's bigger and deals slightly more  damage after a few dozen well-placed  shots in one of its weak points the  Thunder jaw should crumble but once  again be wary of outside interference  because you don't want to get  overwhelmed  [Music]  those are three of the toughest machines  you'll find in the wild and there are  plenty more strategies to take these  down make sure to keep your medicine  pouch stocked up and your Quivers full  and you should be good to go if you want  to see more horizon subscribe and be  sure to check out our new show reboot  it's a weekly editorial show with full  episodes every other Sunday and a Q&amp;A  with Mike McCarty and myself in the off  weeks good luck out there hunters and as  always thanks for watching
 

